  "id": "COMPOUND:4147 - PROTEIN:1849",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 3-Phenylpropylamine and ATP phosphoribosyltransferase through a series of enzymatic pathways. The compound 3-Phenylpropylamine is implicated in targeting Tyrosine-protein phosphatase YopH, which in turn is a target of multiple phosphorylated compounds, including Monoisopropylphosphorylserine and Phenethylamine. All these intermediates ultimately direct their targets to ATP phosphoribosyltransferase, a key enzyme in the biosynthesis of nucleotides. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and moderately strong association, suggesting that 3-Phenylpropylamine may modulate the activity of YopH, which could influence the phosphorylation of other proteins and, consequently, the function of ATP phosphoribosyltransferase. The evidence supports a mechanistic link where 3-Phenylpropylamine may act as a regulator of the phosphoribosyltransferase pathway, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
